\": \"An employee can sign in through the responsive web app using a Folio3 Google Workspace account; successful authentication identifies the employee by corporate email and opens the dashboard.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Personal Gmail accounts, other email providers, and accounts not authorized as Folio3 employees are denied access with an explanatory error; no employee session is created.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For a dedicated parking holder, the system populates and maintains the employee ID, name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details from available employee and parking records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder can have one or more registered vehicles. A non-dedicated employee with no registered vehicle is prompted to enter at least one license plate before proceeding; make, model, and color are optional.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system saves submitted vehicle details for future parking use. Invalid or missing required license plates prevent completion and are reported to the employee.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Returning employees with a completed profile go directly to the dashboard after successful sign-in.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Chosen reading: this is one responsive web app usable in a phone browser, not a native iOS or Android app; mobile-specific notifications are provided as in-app notices or email rather than native push.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder can use a single action on the home screen to release their assigned parking for today; the system confirms success, changes the status to Released, and makes the space available according to the daily release-time rules.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The holder can view the current status, including Reserved, Released, or Claimed by Another Employee, and sees status changes as they occur.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only employees with dedicated parking can release an assigned space; other employees cannot access or perform this action.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A second release attempt for the same space and day is rejected without creating another release.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If another employee has already claimed the released space, the holder is told that it cannot be reclaimed for that day without administrator intervention; the claim remains in force.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder can select one or more dates in the calendar up to 30 days ahead and schedule release of their assigned parking for those dates; the scheduled releases are shown on the calendar and become available for claiming at the applicable release time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects dates outside the allowed 30-day window and prevents employees without dedicated parking from scheduling releases.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The holder can cancel a scheduled release while it remains unclaimed; the cancellation is reflected on the calendar and the space is no longer offered for that date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a scheduled release has already been claimed, cancellation is rejected and the holder is informed that administrator intervention is required to revert it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system records each scheduled release and cancellation in an audit history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An employee without dedicated parking can view the number of parking spaces currently available to claim; dedicated parking holders cannot claim released spaces as temporary parking.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Eligible employees receive an in-app notice or email when spaces become available; the responsive web app displays availability and allows a claim without relying on native push notifications.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Pre-scheduled releases and same-day releases made before the configured Daily Parking Release Time become available at that time (default 8:00 AM); same-day releases made after that time become available immediately.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An eligible employee can claim an available space on a first-come, first-served basis. The system atomically assigns one available space, updates the available count and records the date, time, employee, and assigned parking; the employee is shown the assigned floor and does not choose a specific space.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If no space remains when the claim is processed, including when another employee wins a concurrent claim, the request fails, the employee is told there is no space available, and no duplicate allocation is created.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system does not check whether the employee actually parks on the assigned floor.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For vehicles without a permanent parking sticker, the entrance LPR system reads the plate of an approaching car and checks it against that day's temporary parking authorization; non-car objects such as pedestrians and motorcycles are ignored.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a detected plate has a valid current-day temporary allocation, the system records a successful verification and activates the green indicator so security can allow entry.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When no valid allocation matches, the indicator remains off, the attempt is recorded as unsuccessful, and security does not permit entry.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each verification attempt records date, time, detected plate, verification result, and entry status, including unsuccessful attempts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Vehicles displaying permanent Folio3 parking stickers continue through the existing sticker process and are not stopped for temporary LPR verification, even if the holder released their parking in the app.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system compares daily parking assignments and claims with LPR entry records and stores utilization events with the employee, vehicle, and date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated space is recorded as Unused Dedicated Parking when its holder did not release it and no registered vehicle for the holder is detected entering that day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A temporary allocation is recorded as Unused Temporary Parking when the claimant's registered vehicle is not detected entering on the allocated day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Every Monday morning, the system generates a weekly report and emails it to designated stakeholders. The report includes employees with unused dedicated or temporary allocations, daily and weekly 