text\": \"The system saves registered vehicle details for future sessions. If the employee cannot be matched to a profile or required vehicle registration is incomplete, the system reports what is missing and does not treat setup as complete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Sign-in and profile setup are available in the same responsive web app on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers; phone controls are touch-sized.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated-parking holder can use the home-screen action to release their assigned parking for today; the action is available only to employees with dedicated parking.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On release, the holder receives success confirmation and sees the day's status change to Released; the released space becomes eligible for temporary allocation according to the daily release-time rules.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The holder can view whether today's space is Reserved, Released, or Claimed by another employee, with the status updated when a claim is made.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A holder cannot release the same space more than once for the same day. If the space has already been claimed, the holder is told it cannot be reclaimed that day without administrator intervention.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A non-holder cannot use the release action. An attempted release that cannot be completed leaves the existing status unchanged and reports the failure.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The release action and status are available in the responsive web app, including on a phone browser.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dedicated-parking holder can select one or more dates in the next 30 days and schedule release for those dates; each scheduled release is shown on the calendar and becomes available for claiming at the configured daily release time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The holder can cancel a scheduled release while it has not been claimed; the cancellation is reflected on the calendar and the space is no longer offered for that date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a scheduled space has already been claimed, cancellation is refused and the holder is told that administrator intervention is required to revert it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Past dates and dates more than 30 days ahead cannot be scheduled; invalid selections are rejected without creating a release.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only dedicated-parking holders can schedule or cancel their releases. Each schedule and cancellation is retained in an audit history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Calendar scheduling and cancellation are usable in the responsive web app on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An employee without dedicated parking can view the current count of available spaces and claim an available space; employees with dedicated parking cannot claim temporary parking.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Temporary spaces are offered first-come, first-served: advance releases and same-day releases made before the configured daily release time become claimable at that time, while same-day releases made after it become claimable immediately.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a space becomes available, eligible employees are notified in the web app or by email, and can open the availability view to claim it.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On a successful claim, the system assigns one available space automatically, reduces the available count, displays the assigned parking floor, and records the date, time, employee, and allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If another employee claims the last available space first, or no space is available, the claim is rejected, the employee is shown the current availability, and no duplicate allocation is created.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The employee does not select a specific space, and the system does not verify whether they park on the assigned floor.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Availability and claiming are provided by the responsive web app and work on a phone browser without a native app.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For a vehicle without a permanent Folio3 parking sticker, the entrance system reads its license plate and checks it against that day's temporary parking allocations.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a detected plate has a valid temporary allocation, the system activates the green indicator; the security guard allows entry on seeing the green indicator.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a plate has no valid allocation, the green indicator remains off and the guard does not allow the vehicle to enter.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Vehicles with permanent parking stickers continue through the existing sticker process and are not blocked by a release made in the app; pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects are ignored.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each verification attempt is recorded with its date, time, detected plate, result, and entry status, including unsuccessful attempts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a plate cannot be read or checked, the vehicle is not given temporary authorization and the failed verification outcome is recorded where an attempt was detected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system records parking use from vehicle-entry records and identifies a dedicated allocation as Unused Dedicated Parking when the holder neither released it nor had a registered vehicle detected entering that day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system identifies a temporary allocation as Unused Temporary Parking when the claimant's registered vehicle was not detected entering on the allocation date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Utilization events are retained with the employee, vehicle, and date, and the system tracks daily and weekly utilization, released-space totals, temporary-claim totals, and overall utilization percentage.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A weekly utilization report is generated automatically every Monday morning and emailed to the configured stakeholders; it includes employees with unused dedicated or temporary parking and the utilization and allocation statistics.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A parking administrator can configure the report's designated stakeholders; report generation and delivery do not apply warnings, suspensions, or penalties to employees in Phase 1.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If entry records are absent, the applicable unused-parking event is recorded rather than treated as confirmed use.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat 'unused' as determined from the absence of a registered-vehicle entry record for that day, as described in the request; do not infer penalties or enforcement.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An employee signs in with a Folio3 Google Workspace account; the system authenticates the account and uses the corporate email to identify the employee and retrieve their employee profile.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A personal Gmail account, another email provider, or an account not authorized as a Folio3 employee is refused access and shown an authentication/access error.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For an employee with dedicated parking, the system populates the profile with available employee ID, name, assigned-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details, including one or more license plates and any stored make, model, or color.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On first use, an employee without dedicated parking is prompted to register at least one license plate before proceeding; make, model, and color may also be entered. The system saves the vehicle details for later parking requests.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user with a returning profile who signs in successfully is taken to the dashboard without repeating first-use vehicle registration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The employee accesses the same responsive web application from a phone, tablet, or desktop browser; phone controls are touch-sized. No native-app-only sign-in flow is required.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Folio3 Google Workspace authentication is required; dedicated-holder data is imported from the employee record, while 